  "id": "COMPOUND:23337 - PROTEIN:124",
  "verbalization": "Nanolobatin B appears to exert its biological effects through a shared target, the sodium-dependent proline transporter, which is targeted by multiple compounds (Paeonilide, Bakuchalcone, and (+)-Parviflorol). These compounds are all known to interact with the CD3 zeta chain, a critical component of the T-cell receptor complex. The high scores in the evidence suggest a strong, consistent relationship between Nanolobatin B and the CD3 zeta chain, likely through the same or similar molecular mechanisms. The presence of multiple compounds targeting the same downstream pathway supports the hypothesis that Nanolobatin B may act by modulating the sodium-dependent proline transporter, which in turn affects the CD3 zeta chain. The mechanism is supported by the observed targeting of the transporter by different compounds, indicating a potential role in the regulation of T-cell function. The evidence is robust and aligns with the expected biological role of the CD3 zeta chain in immune signaling, making this a plausible and mechanistically sound relationship.",
